Hypothesis Development
Anthropomorphism refers to the attribution of qualities that are unique to humans (e.g., emotions, language, and actions) to non-human entities (e.g., pets) (Epley et al., 2007). People often display affection towards anthropomorphized entities (e.g., regarding a pet as a child and thus dressing and pampering it), and through these interactions, meet their own needs (e.g., companionship or desire for control) (Eyssel & Reich, 2013). From a commercial perspective, anthropomorphizing a product
