Data Collection
Conversational service models with VAs as the medium are increasingly popular. They are gradually changing how companies interact with customers, and have been applied to a variety of scenarios (e.g., shopping, ticketing, and financial management). The authors therefore adopted convenience sampling (Evans & Mathur, 2005) to administer our survey to consumers with experience in using VA services. The questionnaire was administered electronically via SurveyCake (www.surveycake.com) for six weeks from 28 June 2022 to 9 August 2022. A total of 378 questionnaires were completed. After removing invalid questionnaires (e.g., respondents who never or rarely used VAs), the authors obtained 305 valid questionnaires for analysis. This sample size is in line with the recommendations of Kock and Hadaya (2018) for partial least square structural equation modeling; that is “sample size should be greater than ten times the maximum number of inner or outer model links pointing at any latent variable in the model” (Kock & Hadaya, 2018). Our study has a maximum of five inner links (within the “trust” construct) and five outer links (between the constructs of “trust” and “attitude”). Table 2 presents the demographic data of the respondents. Male respondents accounted for 48.2% of the valid samples. The largest age group contained respondents between the ages of 21 and 25 (17.7%) and the second-largest groups were between the ages of 51 to 55, and 56 to 60 (both 14.4%). About half the respondents (49.2%) had master’s degrees or higher and the next largest group (46.2%) had bachelor’s degrees. With regard to VA usage experience, 80.7% of respondents had used Apple’s Siri, 56.7% had used Google Assistant, and 22.3% had used MI AI; the use of other VAs was less than 10%. Apple’s Siri was most frequently used (63%), followed by Google Assistant (29.5%), and only 7.5% frequently used other VAs. Because the survey was conducted in Taiwan, the distribution of VA use may reflect the first-mover advantage, localization, and the easy availability of Apple and Google in Taiwan. Regarding the frequency of VA use, 38% of people reported using a VA every day and 37.7% reported using a VA several times a week.
DATA ANALYSIS AND RESULTS
The authors adopted the partial least squares (PLS) method and conducted data analysis using SmartPLS 3.3.3. PLS is a form of structural equation modeling (SEM) for statistical analysis that is well-suited to the size of the sample used in this study (i.e., 305 samples). To achieve stability in the various construct estimates, the authors employed bootstrap resampling with a sample size of 5,000 for parameter estimation and inference.
Instrument Validation
First, the authors examined the stability and consistency of model reliability, adopting Cronbach’s α to evaluate the reliability of the constructs (see Appendix). The Cronbach’s α coefficients ranged from 0.777 to 0.881, and were all greater than the standard of 0.7 (Bagozzi & Yi, 1988). Composite reliability (CR) ranged from 0.845 to 0.926, indicating good internal consistency among the constructs. The authors then examined the convergent validity and discriminant validity of the model. The former indicates a high degree of correlation among the observed variables in a single construct, which can then be used to measure the target construct (Churchill Jr., 1979). The factor loadings of some of the question items (HLT1, HLT3, and T3) did not reach the threshold of 0.7 suggested by Hair et al. (2010). However, some researchers have recommended keeping factor loadings greater than 0.6 or between 0.4 and 0.7 for PLS (Chin, 1998; Hulland, 1999; Moores & Chang, 2006). The average variance extracted (AVE) of the constructs all reached the suggested 0.5 (Fornell & Larcker, 1981), thereby indicating good convergent validity. With regard to discriminant validity, the authors followed the suggestions of Fornell and Larcker (1981). That is, the authors checked whether the square root of the AVE of each construct was greater than the coefficients of correlation between constructs and whether all the ratios in the matrix of heterotrait-monotrait ratio (HTMT) were less than 0.85 (Henseler
